 the verdict card below the picture: is this bridge SAFE, MARGINAL, or FAILED, and why?"],["LI",{},"Drag any slider and watch the verdict, the colors, and the numbers respond instantly. Breaking it on purpose is a great way to learn."],["LI",{},"Save your starting design in the notebook. Improve its safety margin, then compare material cost under the same applied load."]],["P",{"style":"font-size: 12px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin: 0px 0px 10px; line-height: 1.6;"},"In every picture: red pieces are being STRETCHED (tension), blue pieces are being SQUEEZED (compression), and thicker means working harder."],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","style":"padding: 6px 12px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.6); background: transparent; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer;"},"Got it — hide this"]],["P",{"style":"color: var(--allo-stem-text, #cbd5e1); font-size: 13px; margin-bottom: 12px; line-height: 1.6;"},"Warren truss bridge stress test. Adjust the parameters below and see how force distribution changes. ",["STRONG",{"style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"Red = tension"],", ",["STRONG",{"style":"color: rgb(125, 211, 252);"},"blue = compression"],", thickness shows magnitude. Forces are solved exactly by the method of joints — every member force satisfies equilibrium at both of its ends."],["DIV",{"style":"margin-bottom: 8px;"},["DIV",{"role":"group","aria-label":"Bridge view","style":"display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 8px;"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"true","style":"padding: 9px 12px; min-height: 40px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgb(100, 116, 139); background: rgb(15, 23, 42); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer;"},"3D structure"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","style":"padding: 9px 12px; min-height: 40px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgb(100, 116, 139); background: rgb(15,