color: var(--allo-stem-text, #e2e8f0);"},["STRONG",{"style":"color: rgb(134, 239, 172); min-width: 150px;"},"✓ Strength (yield)"],["SPAN",{},"Safety factor 5.83 (max stress 60 MPa vs nominal strength 350 MPa)"]],["DIV",{"style":"display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 8px; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--allo-stem-text, #e2e8f0);"},["STRONG",{"style":"color: rgb(252, 165, 165); min-width: 150px;"},"✗ Stability (buckling)"],["SPAN",{},"Governing member TC2: P_cr 93 kN vs compression 300 kN; length 6.7 m; slenderness 327 (pinned ends K=1; solid square section)"]],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--allo-stem-text, #cbd5e1); line-height: 1.6;"},"BUCKLING FAILURE: member TC2 reaches its Euler buckling load before material yield. Long, thin compression members can buckle far below crushing strength. Thicken the section, shorten the unbraced length, add bracing, or revise the geometry."]],["DIV",{"style":"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 12px;"},["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Max chord force"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(248, 113, 113); margin-top: 2px;"},"300 kN"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"The biggest pull or squeeze in the long top/bottom pieces. (1 kN is about the weight of a washing machine.)"]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Max diagonal force"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(96, 165, 250); margin-top: 2px;"},"180 kN"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"The biggest force in the zig-zag pieces. Diagonals work hardest near the supports."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Max stress"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(245, 158, 11); margin-top: 2px;"},"60 MPa"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"Force squeezed into each bit of material. Must stay well BELOW the yield number beside it."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Material yield"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(148, 163, 184); margin-top: 2px;"},"350 MPa"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"The stress where this material starts to permanently bend or tear. Your ceiling."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Buckling load (P_cr)"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(167, 139, 250); margin-top: 2px;"},"93 kN"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"The push at which the weakest strut snaps sideways, like a spaghetti noodle pressed from both ends."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Weakest strut"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(167, 139, 250); margin-top: 2px;"},"TC2"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"The piece closest to buckling. Find it in the picture above; the whole bridge is only as safe as this one piece."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Slenderness ratio (L/r)"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(167, 139, 250); margin-top: 2px;"},"327"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"Length divided by thickness. Long and thin = wobbly. Real design codes stop at about 200."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Push-back at each support"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(148, 163, 184); margin-top: 2px;"},"150 kN"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"How hard each end pushes back up. The two ends together carry the whole load."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Diagonal angle"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(148, 163, 184); margin-top: 2px;"},"56°"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"Changing the angle changes both the member length and force. Compare designs under the same load to see the trade-off."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Total member length"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(148, 163, 184); margin-top: 2px;"},"145.4 m"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"All the pieces laid end to end. More length = more material = more cost."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Estimated mass"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(148, 163, 184); margin-top: 2px;"},"5709 kg"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"What the bare structure weighs. A bridge must carry itself before it carries anything else."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Estimated material cost"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(134, 239, 172); margin-top: 2px;"},"$34252"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"The engineering game: the CHEAPEST design that is still SAFE wins."]]],["DETAILS",{"style":"margin-bottom: 12px; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155); background: var(--allo-stem-panel, #1e293b); padding: 10px 14px;"},["SUMMARY",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: var(--allo-stem-text, #e2e8f0); cursor: pointer;"},"📖 The words on this page, in plain language"],["DL",{"style":"margin: 10px 0px 0px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--allo-stem-text, #cbd5e1); line-height: 1.6; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 8px 18px;"},["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Tension — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"A pulling force, like a tug-of-war rope. Shown in red."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Compression — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"A squeezing force, like pressing on a soda can. Shown in blue."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Truss — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"A frame of triangles. Triangles cannot change shape without changing a side length, which makes them stiff."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Member / chord / diagonal — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"Any single piece is a member. The long top and bottom pieces are chords; the zig-zags are diagonals."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Yield — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"The point where a material stops springing back and permanently bends or tears. Passing it is a strength failure."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Buckling — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"When a long thin piece under squeeze suddenly snaps sideways, far below its crushing strength. Press a spaghetti noodle from both ends to feel it."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Safety factor — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"Calculated capacity divided by the current demand. At 1.0 the model reaches a limit. This lab uses 2.0 as a learning target; real design uses code-specific load and resistance factors."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Governing — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"Engineer-speak for \"the one that decides\". The governing member is the weakest link; the governing check is whichever fails first."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"kN (kilonewton) — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"A unit of force. 1 kN is roughly the weight of a washing machine; a car weighs about 15 kN."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"MPa (megapascal) — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"Pressure: force concentrated on an area. The same push hurts more through a thumbtack than a book cover; that is higher MPa."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Span — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"The open distance the bridge must cross without support underneath."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Slenderness — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"Length compared to thickness. A pencil is stubby; an uncooked spaghetti noodle is slender. Slender pieces buckle easily."]]]],["SECTION",{"style":"padding: 14px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--allo-stem-panel, #1e293b); border-top: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155); border-right: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155); border-left: 3px solid rgb(125, 211, 252); margin-bottom: 12px;"},["H3",{"style":"margin-top: 0px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 800; color: var(--allo-stem-text, #e2e8f0); margin-bottom: 8px;"},"Follow the load"],["DIV",{"data-bridge-inspector":"true"},["P",{"style":"margin: 0px 0px 10px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6;"},"Choose a member to inspect its force and margin. In the labelled 2D view, its identifier marks the same member. Positive forces pull; negative forces compress."],["LABEL",{"for":"bridge-member-select","style":"display: block; margin-bottom: 6px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 12px;"},"Inspect member"],["SELECT",{"id":"bridge-member-select","style":"padding: 9px 12px; min-height: 40px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgb(100, 116, 139); background: rgb(15, 23, 42); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; width: 100%; margin-bottom: 10px;"},["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"BC0"},"BC0 · B0 → B1"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"BC1"},"BC1 · B1 → B2"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"BC2"},"BC2 · B2 → B3"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"BC3"},"BC3 · B3 → B4"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"BC4"},"BC4 · B4 → B5"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"BC5"},"BC5 · B5 → B6"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"TC0"},